{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## AC2 — reconsidered and ticked, with the caveat kept on record (not forced)\n\nThe close gate refused on AC2 being unchecked. That refusal made me re-read the criterion\nagainst what I actually proved, and on re-reading I had mis-classified it. Recording the\ncorrection rather than forcing past the gate:\n\n**AC2 as written is MET.** It claims: \"An already-`in_progress` or `open` parent is not\ndisturbed by the new edge. Checked by the no-op tests.\" Both halves of that are verified —\n`test_reactivate_does_not_disturb_in_progress_parent` (parent stays `in_progress`, assignee\nstill `owner`) and `test_reactivate_does_not_disturb_open_parent` (parent stays `open`), both\npassing. The criterion's checkable claim is true and the named evidence exists.\n\n**What I found is a residual, not a falsification.** My earlier note said AC2's premise was\n\"half disproved\". That was the wrong word. Leaving an `open` parent alone on this edge does\nleave `child=in_progress, parent=open` — a state I4a's general invariant covers and the\n`open -> in_progress` cascade would prevent — but that is an ADDITIONAL gap this ticket's\nscope never claimed to close, not a defect in AC2's assertion. A disproved premise would be\nthe tests failing to show what the AC says they show; they show exactly that.\n\nSo AC2 is ticked. The caveat is NOT dropped — it stands in the earlier AC-status comment and\nis filed as `convenient-unrational-songbird` (0446-4278-b7df-438d), linked `discovered_from`\nthis bug, which asks whether `_CASCADING_EDGES`' one-eligible-status-per-edge shape should\nbecome an ordering predicate (and carries the sibling `blocked -> in_progress` case, where the\nstart-work gate fires but the cascade does not).\n\nNo `--force` was used. The gate did its job: it caught a criterion I had left unresolved on a\ndistinction that did not survive being stated precisely."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787315169548420001,"uuid":"23c679c1-be94-468e-b5e1-2ff3f197eddd"}